WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.449
Step nine turns steps
three to eight into policy,

2
00:00:03.449 --> 00:00:08.462
because drift is the threat, as
Governance, Drift and Evidence explains.

3
00:00:08.462 --> 00:00:13.493
Gather the security definitions into
one initiative at the intermediate root:

4
00:00:13.493 --> 00:00:16.617
DDoS protection on virtual
networks and its logs,

5
00:00:16.617 --> 00:00:20.656
the web application firewall
enabled and in the specified mode,

6
00:00:20.656 --> 00:00:25.076
the private D N S and public-access
policies, and the Key Vault policies.

7
00:00:25.076 --> 00:00:28.112
Look up each definition's
name in the cloud you're in,

8
00:00:28.112 --> 00:00:30.137
because built-ins differ by cloud.

9
00:00:30.137 --> 00:00:32.109
Assign it in do-not-enforce mode,

10
00:00:32.109 --> 00:00:35.749
review compliance with the
owners, then switch to default.

11
00:00:35.749 --> 00:00:38.913
Run a remediation task
for what already exists.

12
00:00:38.913 --> 00:00:41.963
Every exemption gets a
category and an expiry.

13
00:00:41.963 --> 00:00:46.882
Learn's Azure Policy exemption structure
says mitigated means the intent is met

14
00:00:46.882 --> 00:00:50.701
another way, waiver means
non-compliance is accepted for a time,

15
00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:54.887
and an expired exemption is kept for
the record but no longer honored.

16
00:00:54.887 --> 00:00:57.140
Export compliance every month.
